# Fixture: Europe base (60000 gold, tax 6%) with the nation's boycott_bitmap = Tobacco (bit 2); a Galleon in the harbor holds
# Tobacco 100 / Cotton 40 / Tobacco 60. Back taxes = ask (5 bid + 1 burden = 6) x 500 = 3000, credited to royal_money.
# Hold i is at x = 152+12i, y 171; market cell i at x = 10+19i, y 189; @KISSUP rows at y 156 (refuse) and 168 (Pay).
key e                    # open the European Status screen
wait 10
drag 152 171 48 189      # sell refused: boycotted Tobacco raises @KISSUP and the trade is aborted whatever the answer
key Return               # decline @KISSUP (row 0 = refuse): the Tobacco hold stays aboard
key u                    # U sells ONE hold, the lowest key first (FUN_479b_0f60): Cotton 40 (4*16*40) beats Tobacco 60 and 100; 40 @ 4 = 160, tax 9, net 151
key u                    # now the lowest key is the boycotted Tobacco 60: @KISSUP and the sale is aborted, nothing falls through to another hold
key Return               # decline @KISSUP
click 153 155            # the Galleon's icon: ship menu
click 150 109            # row 3 Unload all cargo: every hold left is boycotted Tobacco, so none is sold and @SOMEBOYCOTT is raised (the last-examined slot 0 was boycotted)
key Return               # OK @SOMEBOYCOTT
click 48 189             # the boycotted market cell raises @KISSUP quoting 3000 in back taxes
click 150 156            # first row (decline): nothing changes
key l                    # buy on the selected boycotted Tobacco cell: @KISSUP instead of the @HOWMUCH4 prompt
key Return               # decline: no gold spent, no cargo loaded
click 48 189             # @KISSUP again
click 150 168            # "Pay 3000.": gold -3000, royal_money +3000, boycott bit cleared
drag 176 171 48 189      # Tobacco sells now: 60 @ 4 = 240, tax 14, net 226 (the first Tobacco hold, never sold, stays)
key -                    # '-' sells the whole first hold of the selected cell's good: Tobacco 100 @ 4 = 400, tax 24, net 376
key e                    # leave Europe
